\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4.35}{\ignorespaces Pose tracking against ground truth, 15 November 2026, correction gate at \SI {1.5}{\metre }. Route shapes were driven by hand: straight, approximately square, approximately a figure-of-eight. ``Over 1\,m'' is the longest unbroken stretch with the error above a metre and ``ended'' the median over the last tenth of the run, i.e. whether it came back. Offset and scatter, reported in the text, are \SIrange {0.04}{0.34}{\metre } and \SIrange {0.03}{0.19}{\metre } respectively. Blind is the share of localisation poses carrying RTAB-Map's no-information covariance. Ground truth is compared without a lever arm, for the reason given under Frames.\relax }}{136}{table.caption.247}%
